codex
Findings:

- `scripts/extract_to_ssot.py:153` and `scripts/extract_to_ssot.py:195` — ZERO CONFLATED WITH ABSENT.  
  Input: `t={"identity":{"id":"T1"},"effect":{"estimate":0.0,"variance":0.0,"measure":"HR"}}`; call `_per_trial(t,"log",{})` or `_trial_effect(t,"log")`.  
  Consequence: `variance=0.0` produces `se=None`, so the derived CI becomes `None` instead of the exact zero-width interval.

- `scripts/extract_to_ssot.py:242` — ABSENT SCALE CONVERTED INTO A VALUE.  
  Input state: `trials=[{"effect":{"estimate":2.0,"variance":0.04}}]`, `rep={"logEffect":2.0,"lci":1.0,"uci":3.0}`.  
  Consequence: missing scale silently becomes `"log"`, so natural-scale values are exponentiated instead of refused.

- `scripts/extract_to_ssot.py:314` — ZERO / NULL EFFECT MISCLASSIFIED.  
  Input state: `scale="log"`, `pt=1.0`, reached from `rep={"logEffect":0.0,"lci":0.0,"uci":0.0}`.  
  Consequence: a null ratio effect is reported as `favours="control"` rather than neutral/unknown.

- `scripts/extract_to_ssot.py:357` — CHECK THAT CANNOT FAIL for non-NCT registration IDs.  
  Input: `subject_match({"inputs":{"trials":[{"trial_id":"ISRCTN12345678"}]}},{"canonical":{}})`.  
  Consequence: the “HARD GATE” returns `0` and accepts a foreign registration identifier because it only searches `NCT\d{8}`.

- `scripts/extract_to_ssot.py:81` — NEGATION DROPPED.  
  Input: `withdrawn_pages('<a href="X.html" class="card util"><span class="name">X</span><span class="pub">not withdrawn</span></a>')`.  
  Consequence: `X.html` is treated as withheld even though the status sentence negates withdrawal.

No proven finding in this file for: probe keyed to a fix-removed string; own-comment idempotency guard; CRLF/LF text comparison; merged-cell tabulation; wrapper status-code reporting.
